This is the sic fork of musl libc.

Upstream musl (https://musl.libc.org, release 1.2.5) is Copyright (c) 2005-2020
Rich Felker et al. and MIT licensed; see COPYRIGHT, which applies unchanged to
every upstream file, including the ones modified below. The sic changes on top
of it are Copyright (C) 2026 Rigby Foundation and licensed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 2.1 or later (see LICENSE), so that programs
linking this libc — statically, as everything on sic does — are not affected:

  arch/x86_64/bits/syscall.h.in   sic's system call numbers (generated from
                                  sic/abi/syscall.tbl in the kernel tree)
  arch/x86_64/syscall_arch.h      no vDSO
  src/thread/x86_64/clone.s, __set_thread_area.s, __unmapself.s,
  src/signal/x86_64/restore.s, src/process/x86_64/vfork.s
                                  hard-coded syscall numbers
  include/linux/fb.h              framebuffer ioctls: forwards to the kernel's
                                  abi/fb.h (Linux-shaped, so fbdev code ports)
  arch/powerpc/bits/syscall.h.in, src/thread/powerpc/clone.s, __unmapself.s,
  src/signal/powerpc/restore.s   the same for the 32-bit PowerPC port
  src/sic/builtins.c              64-bit division/shift helpers the compiler
                                  expects from libgcc on 32-bit targets
  GNUmakefile, README.md, NOTICE, LICENSE

Everything else is unmodified upstream musl.
